From d53abc70c032f29bf107e6b6c8fcf52d685bc47b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 08:26:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 81/83] build: scripted, reproducible cross-sysroot mirroring
 (scripts/sync-sysroot.sh)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The libs+headers mirroring into the cross-toolchain sysroot lived inline in
build.sh and only ran during a full contrib build, so a sysroot that was
fresh (or whose packages were built out-of-band) was left incomplete — the
GTK+2 stack runtime worked but its headers/libs were absent from
/opt/substrate/i386-unknown-substrate, so the cross compiler couldn't build
new GTK+2 apps.

Extract the logic into scripts/sync-sysroot.sh: standalone and idempotent,
it reconstructs the sysroot from the existing dist-<pkg>/ outputs (and the
native lib/, usr.lib/, include/ trees) WITHOUT a rebuild, so CI/automation
can run it any time.  build.sh now sources it and calls the same
sync_to_sysroot()/sync_native_libs_to_sysroot() functions during a build —
one source of truth, no duplication.

Running it mirrors all 104 dist trees; verified the full GTK+2 stack
(libpng/freetype/cairo/pango/atk/gdk-pixbuf/gtk-x11 + their versioned
include subdirs) now resolves, and a cross-compile of `#include <gtk/gtk.h>`
+ gtk_init() parses through the complete glib/gobject/gio/gtk chain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
